Package: ctPWAS
Type: Package
Title: Cell-Type-Level Proteomics-Wide Association Studies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Sinan",
           family = "Zhu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "sinan.zhu@u.duke.nus.edu"),
    person(given = "Xiaoyu",
           family = "Song",
           role = "ths",
           email = "song.xiaoyu@duke-nus.edu.sg"))
Description: Performs cell-type-specific proteome-wide association studies (PWAS) using bulk tissue proteomic data and GWAS summary statistics. By modeling bulk protein abundance as a mixture of multiple cell types, ctPWAS estimates cell-type-specific genetic prediction weights and identifies protein–trait associations at both cell-type and tissue levels. The package provides tools to (1) estimate sample-level cell-type proportions using marker-protein-guided deconvolution; (2) train cell-type-specific elastic-net prediction models with mirror-statistic-based stability screening; and (3) perform cell-type-specific and joint association tests using GWAS summary statistics and a linkage disequilibrium reference panel, with the aggregated Cauchy association test (ACAT) for combining evidence across cell types. ctPWAS extends MiXcan to accommodate more than two cell types and enables association testing without individual-level GWAS genotypes.
URL: https://github.com/songxiaoyu/ctPWAS
